{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgmeKH2EGW7ZsE3mcQKc6","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Here's what I'd tell my son on the phone.\n\nI didn't decide anything. I'll go to the bank and ask them, and I'll ask you too. I'm fairly sure of only one thing. The page says that if more than 15,000 ₪ sits in the עו\"ש for a whole quarter, \"הבנק חייב לשלוח לכם הודעה שמפנה לחלופות\". I never got a letter like that, or maybe I didn't notice it. Either way, it's a fair question for the clerk. The page never told me how much my account costs. It only says the fee is \"לפי התעריפון של הגורם המציע\", with no number.\n\n**What I looked at, in order:**\n1. **The top.** The heading \"חשבון עובר ושב\" is something I know, so I stayed. The text says not every bank pays interest on money in the account, and that a bank that pays none has to say so. There are fee \"tracks\": the basic one includes 1 action at a teller and 10 online, the extended one 10 and 50. I didn't know I could ask for the basic one.\n2. **The calculator.** The first big number was \"74,044 ₪\". It used 10,000 ₪ plus 500 ₪ a month and 5% a year. I don't understand why a current account would earn 5% when the page itself says these accounts often pay no interest. There's a little sentence saying it's \"דוגמה, לא תחזית\". I didn't look at the chart or the sliders.\n3. **Why people use it.** There's a sentence about \"קרן כספית יומית\" being better than the עו\"ש unless you need the money the same day. I don't know what that is, and I won't put money into something I don't know.\n4. **\"שווה לדעת\".** One line there says \"אין ביטוח פיקדונות\". That frightened me.\n5. **The cost section.** There's a table with no amounts in it at all.\n6. **Tax.** Something about 15% and 25%. I skimmed it.\n7. **\"סיכונים ומה לא מוגן\".** It says there is no deposit insurance in Israel. If a bank fails, the Bank of Israel governor steps in, but it's \"לא זכות שלכם\". There's a proposal for 250,000 ₪, and it says even that wouldn't include the עו\"ש. That worried me a lot about my deposits too.\n\n**What I didn't read:** the boxes about withdrawals and switching tracks, and the section \"מה האתר לקח בחשבון\", which had little lock signs and \"שאלה פתוחה\". I only glanced at the word list (\"מונחים\") on the sixth screen. By then I was tired and stopped. I never opened the seventh screen.\n\n**Words and signs I didn't understand:**\n- BANK-20, BANK-23, BANK-15, TXI OQ11, BANK OQ9\n- \"קרן כספית\", \"מק\"מ\", \"יתרת זכות\" (I think it means the money I have in the account)\n- \"הצמדה: לא צמוד\"\n- \"מזומן שקלי\"\n- the small purple box \"מחושב\"\n- the \"123\" numbers with the coloured underlines at the top\n\nThere was a red box with \"שאלה פתוחה\" that I couldn't make sense of. The grey writing on the black background was hard to read even enlarged, especially the small notes under the calculator.\n\n**What bothered me:**\n- I've never heard of this \"מקור\" site.\n- Black screens tire me.\n- Saying there's no deposit insurance scared me more than it helped.\n- It never answered how much my bank is actually taking from me."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3837,"cache_read_input_tokens":11576,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3837},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"df63554b-2a81-41e4-bfb4-680d0fe6511f","uuid":"050e8ccc-c10e-4df5-a80b-ee907c3c83be","timestamp":"2026-11-06T12:05:34.794Z","request_id":"req_011CgmeKGpKyxGbUHLKsvr2S"}
